    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499910/administrative-program-support-3": {
      "title": "Administrative Program Support 3",
      "description": "Administrative Program Support 3 Apply now Search #: 499910 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources (CAHNR) Business Office at the University of Connecticut announces the opening of a full-time Administrative Program Support 3 to support Human Resources and Payroll functions. The incumbent will work under the limited supervision of the Assistant Dean for Finance and Administration and will provide independent administrative support for a broad range of Human Resources activities, with additional responsibility for selected Payroll processes. The position serves as a resource to CAHNR departments, faculty, staff, and administrators and works closely with central University offices to support accurate, timely, and compliant personnel administration. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES HUMAN RESOURCES Serves as a resource to CAHNR administrators, faculty, staff, and supervisors on routine and moderately complex Human Resources policies, procedures, and personnel actions, escalating unusual or sensitive matters to the Assistant Dean, Human Resources, or other appropriate University offices. Supports supervisors with the documentation and routing of routine personnel and employee relations matters as appropriate. Coordinates and reviews Human Resources transactions for accuracy, completeness, and compliance, including position requests, regular payroll searches, offer letters, continuation letters, Special Payroll requests, temporary service in a higher-class requests, and related personnel actions. Coordinates CAHNR regular payroll offer and continuation letter processes, including preparing, reviewing, routing, tracking, and maintaining documentation and standardized templates. Supports efforts to improve consistency and efficiency in offer letter and continuation processes across departments. Supports UCPEA Career Progression processes by maintaining eligibility and tracking information, coordinating required documentation, communicating deadlines and requirements, assisting employees and supervisors with process questions, and maintaining related records and resources. Coordinates graduate assistant offer letter processes in Slate, including monitoring departmental submissions, reviewing materials for completeness, routing or approving items within delegated authority, tracking outstanding actions, and communicating requirements to department administrators. Coordinates and supports regular payroll searches and recruitment processes in PageUp, including reviewing submissions for completeness, approving or routing transactions within delegated authority, supporting search administration, and communicating with departments, Human Resources, and other University offices as needed. Supports employee onboarding, transfers, and separations, including new employee orientation coordination, onboarding documentation, I-9 processes, personnel record maintenance, organizational chart updates, and related administrative requirements. Supports employment-based immigration processes, including H-1B and J-1 related actions and other visa matters within the scope of the position. Coordinates documentation, communicates with departments and employees, tracks deadlines, and works with International Services, Labor Relations, and other University partners as appropriate. Supports staffing and position administration activities, including staff refills, position justifications, classification related documentation, reclassification and temporary assignment processes, employee separations, and other personnel changes. Helps departments understand required documentation and University processes. Stays current on University policies, collective bargaining agreements, and changes to Human Resources practices and systems. Translates relevant changes into practical guidance, templates, checklists, and training for CAHNR administrative staff and supervisors. Maintains and oversees the maintenance of electronic personnel records and related shared resources, ensuring appropriate organization, accessibility, confidentiality, and records management practices. PAYROLL Reviews and approves designated Core CT payroll transactions within delegated authority, ensuring accuracy and appropriate supporting documentation. Identifies discrepancies and coordinates corrections with departments and/or faculty, the Business Office, Payroll, Human Resources, and other University offices as needed. Assists with routine payroll administration, including pending payroll transactions, employee funding or appointment documentation, and other recurring payroll processes. Provides support in resolving routine payroll questions and escalates complex issues appropriately. Compiles and maintains Human Resources and Payroll data and prepares routine reports, trackers, and summaries used to monitor personnel activity, deadlines, vacancies, appointments, and other operational needs. Monitors employee appointment and funding end dates through recurring payroll review processes; identifies personnel requiring payroll authorizations, extensions, or other employment actions and communicates upcoming deadlines and required actions to departments to support timely payroll processing and continuity of employment. PROCESS IMPROVEMENT, TRAINING, AND COLLABORATION Assesses assigned administrative workflows and recommends process improvements that increase consistency, efficiency, accuracy, and compliance. Develops and maintains job aids, templates, standard operating procedures, and other resources to support department self-service. Serves as a functional resource for Human Resources and Payroll systems used within CAHNR, assisting departments with system processes, troubleshooting routine issues, and coordinating resolution of more complex matters with central offices. Provides ongoing training and guidance to CAHNR administrative staff and new employees on applicable Human Resources and Payroll processes, University systems, and procedural requirements. Represents the CAHNR Business Office in regular College administrative meetings and serves as a liaison with departments and central University offices on Human Resources and Payroll matters. May supervise and evaluate the work of student labor employees and coordinate assigned work to support Business Office operations. Performs additional duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field. Three to four years of related experience in Human Resources administration, personnel administration, payroll administration, or a closely related area. Demonstrated knowledge of Human Resources administration, onboarding processes, and personnel records management. Demonstrated experience interpreting and applying University policies, procedures, collective bargaining requirements, and other applicable standards while exercising sound judgment and discretion. Experience working in a complex, fast paced, multifaceted administrative environment with multiple competing priorities. Experience working independently under limited supervision while collaborating effectively with supervisors, colleagues, departments, and central University offices. Organizational skills and attention to detail, with demonstrated experience managing deadlines, tracking multiple actions, and maintaining accurate records. Demonstrated professional written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated experience maintaining confidentiality and exercising appropriate professional judgment when handling sensitive personnel information. Experience with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in higher education, particularly in an academic or decentralized administrative environment. Experience interpreting or working within a collective bargaining environment. Experience with UConn Core CT, PageUp, Slate, or similar enterprise Human Resources, payroll, recruitment, or document management systems. Experience supporting UCPEA or other career progression, classification, reclassification, or employee development processes. Experience supporting employment-based immigration or visa processes. Demonstrated experience identifying process improvements and developing practical tools, templates, checklists, or training resources. Demonstrated experience establishing effective working relationships with individuals across varied academic, professional, cultural, and organizational backgrounds. Demonstrated experience identifying and resolving problems efficiently and effectively while knowing when to seek guidance. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $60,500 to $78,541. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499910 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. The review of applications will begin immediately and remain ongoing until the position is filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499888/assistant-director-operations-business-operations-specialist-3": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Operations - Business Operations Specialist 3",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Operations - Business Operations Specialist 3 Apply now Search #: 499888 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The School of Fine Arts seeks qualified applicants for a full-time position as Business Operations Specialist 3 (Job Level 5) within the Office of the Dean. Under the direction of the Assistant Dean and COO, this position provides cross-functional operational and technical support to all areas of the School of Fine Arts and is primarily responsible for compensation and budgeting analysis, hiring administration, and serves as a key member to support financial and management reporting, developing and supporting a culture of evidence, assessment, and continuous quality improvement by working collaboratively on optimization projects with key stakeholders and partners. The ideal candidate is a self-motivated, detail-oriented individual capable of working in a fast-paced shared service setting. The School of Fine Arts is committed to being a welcoming community that reflects and enacts the values of diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging. We seek skilled, engaged candidates who will enhance our representational diversity and contribute to diverse, equitable, inclusive, and belonging environments throughout the University. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Manage financial consolidation, data analysis, and preparation of planning materials for headcount and compensation in support of the annual budgeting and quarterly forecasting processes. Track and model compensation expenses, reconcile discrepancies, and ensure policy compliance. Conduct compensation analyses and develop modeling tools for budget preparation, ad hoc reporting, quarterly projections, and long-range forecasts. Manages school-level hiring administration and processing of personnel transactions: appointments, employment changes, leaves, separations, and organizational adjustments. Provides direct support for the School’s hiring and appointments in accordance with governing policies and the associated budget. Works in tandem with the hiring department and Financial Services Office to ensure HR/Payroll activities are contained within the established budgets and processed in accordance with appropriate procedural/approval workflows. Provides guidance to departments on a wide range of human resources topics/acts as a liaison between hiring departments, new hires, and University Human Resources to resolve issues related to hiring, compliance, etc. Collaborate with the Financial Shared Services Office to process transactions related to new hires, attrition replacements, backfills, title changes, transfers, and salary adjustments. Oversee building and space management for the School of Fine Arts and serve as point of contact for facility projects and issues. Coordinate with Facilities Operations and the COO on project updates, policy maintenance, space documentation, emergency plans, and compliance initiatives. Administer the school-wide card reader system and ensure facilities meet safety and accessibility standards. Supervise assigned staff, prioritize tasks, provide training, and monitor performance. Lead or support special projects requiring planning and coordination. Draft and research policies and procedures and perform other assigned duties. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, or related field or a comparable degree. Four (4) or more years of combined experience in workforce planning, budget and headcount analysis with demonstrated experience in financial modeling, data analysis, and statistical forecasting, preferably in a higher education environment. Exceptional analytical skills with attention to detail and strong problem-solving abilities. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with peers, leadership, and subordinates. Consistently strong interpersonal skills and the ability to build and sustain effective working relationships with colleagues of diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Proven ability to efficiently manage multiple high-priority projects, timelines and deliverables. Demonstrated leadership experience. Advanced working knowledge of Excel. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in related field with six to seven years of related experience. Experience with data management systems and data integration. Expertise in financial analysis and data visualization software, such as Power BI or Tableau. Experience in working with Kuali Financial Systems and KFDM/Webfocus or related enterprise GL/reporting systems. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $75,786 to $81,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent, 12-month position with an anticipated start date on or before January 22, 2027. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499888 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 27, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 27 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499684/ovpr-research-facility-specialist": {
      "title": "OVPR Research Facility Specialist",
      "description": "OVPR Research Facility Specialist Apply now Search #: 499684 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Laboratory and Research Operations, Research JOB SUMMARY The Research Infrastructure Unit of the Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) seeks a Facility Professional/P3 to serve as a primary contact for all facility operations in OVPR Research Buildings with a primary focus at the Innovation Partnership Building (IPB). This position serves as a resource for faculty, staff, students, and facilities staff by providing oversight of building functions, serving as a liaison between occupants and Facility Operations, Inventory Control, Key Control, Custodial Services, Buildings and Grounds, Environmental Health and Safety, and Public Safety. This position ensures smooth research operations in the midst of ongoing and future mechanical, plumbing, utility, and automated systems adjustments and throughout building maintenance procedures. Reporting directly to the Facilities Manager in the OVPR Research Infrastructure Unit, this position provides critical scientific support services for faculty, staff and students engaged in a variety of research types. This position supports the Facility Manager in carrying out research support duties in other OVPR Research Buildings including, but not limited to, Science One as needed. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as initial point of contact for building occupants for all routine and emergency maintenance and repair requests: Walks the building daily to monitor condition of building and facilities. Works with faculty and staff to identify, evaluate and/or fix building problems. Initiates work orders to Facilities Operations to describe, correct and follow-up on issues. Works with facilities personnel to give them access to space when needed. Responds to emergencies and facilitate emergency repairs; serve as primary emergency contact 24 hours a day/365 days per year (except during approved time off). Responsible for building security, including maintenance of keys and the electronic security system; work closely with Key Control Department. Monitors and interact with the Building Management System, requiring knowledge of a Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS) such as the Facilities Asset Management Information System (FAMIS), or similar. Maintains cleanliness and appearance and ensures proper security and safety of Innovation Partnership Building loading dock: assists with large deliveries and returns. Maintains the material/equipment parking, attic spaces, and other workshops; ensure accessibility for temporary storage of equipment between delivery to the IPB and its installation elsewhere. Performs installations, alterations and repair of existing furniture/cabinetry/racks, etc. Prepares rooms/laboratories as they are repurposed, which includes removing equipment, furniture, office and laboratory supplies, etc.; coordinates and provides oversight of renovation work performed by others such as Facilities Academic Renovations. Performs and/or assists with small equipment repair and/or the assessment of whether the repairs should be performed by external or internal technical services providers. In collaboration with the Lab Services and Safety Manager, may install or provide assistance with the installation of laboratory equipment. Purchases materials and supplies for maintenance and renovation projects; maintain standing orders with vendors. Applies knowledge of hazardous material safety and handling information as it relates to duties of the Building Manager. Assists the Department Safety Committee and IPB Laboratory Safety Technician in developing appropriate presentations on safety-related building issues and proper maintenance of building infrastructure (e.g. house vacuum, recirculating chilled water, steam, house air, house nitrogen, etc.). Monitors the house liquid nitrogen tank, argon and filling station; refills the large liquid nitrogen Dewars. Prepares and communicates via email building-related issues to building occupants. Serves as an Asset Manager: Serves as primary contact to Inventory Control. Labels, records and tracks all assets using KFS; performs the annual physical inventory audits. Records, organizes and monitors the disposal of tagged equipment; organizes the disposal of non-tagged materials. Assists the IPB Laboratory Safety Technician to maintain, monitor, and ensure proper safety and security of scientific lab equipment. Provides similar support to Science One or other OVPR building occupants as requested. Performs related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in a related field and at least 3 years of demonstrated related experience, knowledge, and skills in a variety of trades such as HVAC, plumbing, electrical and mechanical systems that are relevant to the efficient and effective operation of a large building (e.g. 200,000 sf), its mechanical systems and equipment or a combination of training and experience. An equivalent combination of education and/or experience may be considered. Carpentry experience and working knowledge of a variety of hand and power tools and equipment. Experience in specifying and purchasing parts or equipment. Experience with the Microsoft office suite (particularly spreadsheets, basic word processing and presentation software). Demonstrated verbal and written communications skills. Demonstrated interpersonal skills. Experience working cooperatively and constructively with diverse constituents, such as students, faculty, and staff, and building and maintaining positive relationships. Experience assessing and managing the needs of constituents, communicating those needs to management and staff, and evaluating operations and services to resolve or mitigate issues. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Previous experience serving as a building manager in an academic or industry setting. Experience utilizing job-appropriate online databases and tools (such as KUALI, FAMIS, etc.). COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $60,416 to $78,541. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT The successful incumbent must be willing and able to work occasional weekend and evening hours as needed and able to be on call to report to work during emergency closures, inclement weather, or for significant events that affect building operations and functionality. The successful incumbent must be able to move and lift containers weighing up to 50 pounds to and from locations varying in height from 10 to 36 inches. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499684 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 13, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 13 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
